# FileSwitch as a filing system sees it: a logging filing system
# registered from application space twice, as TxLog (loads and saves
# through Open) and TxRaw (through File 255 and File 0), records each
# entry call — its reason, the names it is handed, counts and offsets,
# never an address, a handle or the time — and answers by the name's last
# character: `$` or `d` a directory, `f` a file of 1000 bytes, buffered in
# 256-byte blocks, `u` an untyped file of 300 bytes, unbuffered.

scenario fileswitch-registration
block fs 5120
write $fs+&0 w=&00000060 w=&0000006C w=&00000354 w=&000006A8 w=&0000073C w=&000005F0 w=&000007A8 w=&00000244 w=&801800FA w=&000003E4 w=&000007D4 w=&00000000 w=&00000066 w=&0000006C w=&00000354 w=&000006A8 w=&0000073C w=&000005F0 w=&000007A8 w=&00000244 w=&800000FB w=&000003E4 w=&000007D4 w=&00000000 w=&6F4C7854 w=&78540067 w=&00776152 w=&78540600 w=&63736944 w=&706C6100 w=&62006168 w=&66617465
